NAME
       cp - copy files and directories

SYNOPSIS
       cp [OPTION]... SOURCE DEST
       cp [OPTION]... SOURCE... DIRECTORY

DESCRIPTION
       Copy SOURCE to DEST, or multiple SOURCEs into DIRECTORY. Permissions of
       the source are kept.

OPTIONS
       -r, -R, --recursive
           copy directories recursively

       -p
           preserve modification and access times

       -a
           archive mode, same as -rp

       -n
           do not overwrite an existing file

       -i
           prompt before overwrite

       -f
           force; accepted for compatibility

       -v
           explain what is being done

       -t DIR
           copy all SOURCE arguments into DIR

EXAMPLES
       cp notes.txt /root/backup/
       cp -rv /usr/share/man /root/man-copy

SEE ALSO
       mv(1), rm(1), install(1)
